    "knowledge_point": "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function in a Given Context",
    "problem": "The function $U(t)$ models the number of users of a new mobile phone app, $t$ hours after launching the app. What is the best interpretation of ${U}^{′}(4)=650?$",
    "worked_solution": "The function ${U}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of users is changing at the moment $t$ hours after launch. \n\nTherefore, ${U}^{′}(4)=650$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour*",
